From 15f9966befdbcd95b34df6242967f84985b95bb0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Petr=20P=C3=ADsa=C5=99?= <ppisar@redhat.com>
Date: Thu, 18 May 2017 15:00:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix building on Perl 5.25.1
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

v5.25.0-71-g5d32d26 enabled PERL_OP_PARENT and that changed op_sibling
semantics for last sibling OP.

As discused in
<https://rt.perl.org/Public/Bug/Display.html?id=128179#txn-1405910>,
updating ppport.h with Devel::PPPort 3.33 and converting the XS code
to use OpSIBLING() helps.

This patch updates ppport.h to 3.36 version and adjusts the XS code.

https://github.com/tokuhirom/B-Tap/issues/4
Signed-off-by: Petr Písař <ppisar@redhat.com>
---
 ppport.h      | 1967 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----------------
 smartmatch.xs |    2 +-
 2 files changed, 1407 insertions(+), 562 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ppport.h b/ppport.h
index 4c042bb..68ec473 100644
--- a/ppport.h
+++ b/ppport.h
@@ -4,9 +4,9 @@
